        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 1089,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:37:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1074,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1090,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153362,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 1090,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:37:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1075,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1091,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153363,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 1091,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Virtually all cases arise in pelviperineal subcutaneous tissue, with most arising in the vulva. About 10&ndash;15% of cases are located in the vagina. Lesions in men occur rarely {10672053; 37389007}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:37:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1076,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1092,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153364,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 1092,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients typically present with a painless, slowly growing subcutaneous mass/swelling misinterpreted as a cyst {1314521; 9308729}. Occasional tumours are pedunculated {22371044}. Angiomyofibroblastoma is usually smaller than 50&nbsp;mm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:37:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1077,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1093,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153365,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 1093,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiomyofibroblastoma is a rare benign soft tissue tumour that most frequently affects the lower genital tract of young to middle-aged women {16943862}. Patients are commonly of reproductive age {8685229; 9308729}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:37:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1078,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1094,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153366,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 1094,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:37:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1079,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1095,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153367,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 1095,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This neoplasm is thought to derive from the subepithelial mesenchyme of the lower genital tract. Most angiomyofibroblastomas harbour recurrent <em>MTG1</em><em>::CYP2E1</em> fusion transcripts {34385605; 36177509}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:37:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1086,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1102,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153368,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 1102,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most tumours are well demarcated, usually unencapsulated lesions; a thin pseudocapsule can be seen. The cut surface is tan-white and solid {1314521; 7551008; 9308729}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:37:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1080,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1096,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153369,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 1096,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiomyofibroblastoma has alternating hypocellular and hypercellular areas and prominent small to medium-sized thin-walled vessels; thick-walled, often hyalinized vessels, can be seen. Stroma is variably myxoedematous to fibrous (fine fibrils or sclerotic plaques) {1314521; 7551008; 8685229; 9308729}. Tumour cells are bland-looking, spindled to ovoid and epithelioid, arranged singly or in small nests or cords, and tend to be clustered around blood vessels. Binucleated and multinucleated cells can be present. Mitoses are rare or absent. Mast cells and lymphocytes can be sparsely observed in the stroma. Intratumoural mature adipocytes can be focal or (in rare examples) nearly diffuse (lipomatous angiomyofibroblastoma) {15782077; 24880711}. Sarcomatous transformation has been suggested by a case report describing the tumour merging imperceptibly with a high-grade sarcoma {9298888}. By immunohistochemistry, the majority of cases show positive staining for desmin, whereas SMA and pan-muscle actin are variably expressed {1314521;24880711}. Desmin staining may be reduced or absent in cases in postmenopausal women. Tumour cells are consistently positive for ER and PR and occasionally positive for CD34.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:37:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1081,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1097,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153370,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 1097,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In one reported case, smears have shown scattered plump, spindle-shaped, and epithelioid cells with oval, bland, vesicular nuclei along with some multinucleated giant cells against a haemorrhagic background {19697746}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:37:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1082,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1098,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153371,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 1098,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Detection of <em>MTG1</em><em>::CYP2E1 </em>fusion can support the diagnosis {36177509; 34385605}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:37:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1085,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1101,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153372,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 1101,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> well-circumscribed tumour; prominent small to medium-sized blood vessels with clustered cytologically bland spindled to ovoid/epithelioid tumour cells; infrequent to absent mitotic figures.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:37:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1083,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1099,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153373,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 1099,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:37:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1084,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1100,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153374,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 1100,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is no potential for recurrence, although 1&nbsp;case associated with sarcomatous transformation locally recurred 2&nbsp;years after initial excision {9298888}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:37:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]